{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:FluidDynamics.NsObstruction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"FluidDynamics.NsObstruction","imports":["lean:module:Init"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:ns_regular_implies_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"ns_regular_implies_zero","kind":"theorem","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/ns-obstruction.lean#L27-L30","doc":"A categorically NS-regular quantum universe has vanishing global obstruction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:NSObstruction.degree_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"NSObstruction.degree_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/ns-obstruction.lean#L25-L25","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:NSObstruction.degree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"NSObstruction.degree","kind":"def","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/ns-obstruction.lean#L24-L24","doc":"Magnitude of the global Euler class degree (0 iff regular). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:NSObstruction.isRegular","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"NSObstruction.isRegular","kind":"def","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/ns-obstruction.lean#L22-L22","doc":"Whether the global surface obstruction class vanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:NSObstruction.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"NSObstruction.mk","kind":"ctor","line":20,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/ns-obstruction.lean#L20-L20","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:NSObstruction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"NSObstruction","kind":"structure","line":4,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/ns-obstruction.lean#L4-L25","doc":"The **NS obstruction class** of a quantum universe `(C, A, τ)` over a\nspectral surface `S`.\n\nPer owner decision Q-VO9T-2 = 1 (2026-11-15, beans `qou-nzyr`, `qou-hjl0`,\nmatching `QOU.FluidDynamics.qou_ns_in_qou` and `def:ns-regular-qou`),\n`NS(A) := e(ξ) ∈ H²(S, ℤ) ≅ ℤ` is the global surface Euler class of the\nReeb bundle `ξ` (with degree `|χ(A)|` tracked here as `degree : Nat`).\n\n- `NS(A) = 0` (`degree = 0`) ⟺ the quantum universe is categorically\n  NS-regular (`isRegular = true`).\n- `NS(A) ≠ 0` (`degree ≠ 0`) ⟺ the quantum universe is categorically\n  NS-singular (`isRegular = false`).\nConnecting these internal categorical labels to classical 3D unforced\nNavier–Stokes regularity or blowup is a framework model correspondence, not\na deductive PDE theorem (Tao's averaged-NS barrier, J. Amer. Math. Soc. 29\n(2016), 601–674). ","signatureChunk":0}]}